<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călēdŏnĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>f</i>, also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călī-</span></b> 
			cf. Welsh celydd, a woody shelter, and Lat. celo, =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καληδονία</span>, <i>the
				province of the ancient Britons</i>, now <i>the
				Highlands in the northern part of Scotland</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. Agr.
			10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25</span></i>;
			31.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călē-dŏnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Caledonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">silva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 16, 30, § 102</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 10, 18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					1, 17, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ursus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Spect. 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Britanni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 44, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Luc. 6, 68</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oceanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val. Fl.
					1, 8</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călēdŏnĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Caledonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">angulus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 22, 1</span></i>
			.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Călēdŏnes</span></b> ,
			um, m., <i>a people in the
				Scottish Highlands</i>, <i><span class="en">Eum. Pan. Const.
				7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
